+// Column widths of an Excel workbook as Excel PRINTS them (BUG-92 horizontal page splits): a column of w characters prints at w times the digit advance of the Normal font at its
+// size, rounded to a whole 1/600 inch (measured on the Office reference: 75 workbooks, 15 fonts, 5 sizes). Returns that digit width in twips (a fraction: k x 2.4), or 0 when the
+// environment variable LO_WASM_EXCEL_PRINT_ROWS is not "1" or the font or size is not covered (the caller then keeps the width it measured on the substitute font).
+SC_DLLPUBLIC double GetExcelColumnDigitTwips(const OUString& rFontName, double fHeightPt);
+
 // A4-declared Excel sheets printed in Letter mode (owner decision 2026-11-14: follow the Office reference). Excel paginates the sheet ON A4 and scales every A4 page onto
 // the Letter page. Calc lays the sheet out exactly as on A4 (100 %: the same rows and columns on each page, the same cell text layout) and the PDF export draws that A4
 // page scaled and shifted onto a Letter page: getRenderer reports the Letter page size and a "ScWasmPageTransform" property that filter/source/pdf/pdfexport.cxx applies
